## 2. Critical & High Severity Issues

Below is a detailed breakdown of the most critical issues identified during the audit, complete with code analysis, impact evaluations, and recommended fixes.

```carousel
### [Critical] Cart Query & Type Mismatch
- **File:** [carts.dart](file:///c:/solcafe/lib/working%20with%20cart/carts.dart#L37-L43) and [cart_service.dart](file:///c:/solcafe/lib/cart%20services/cart%20service.dart)
- **Problem:**
  The cart queries filter by matching `userId` to a `DocumentReference` to `/users/uid`. However, the model saves `userId` as a plain `String`. Additionally, `carts.dart` casts `itemId` (which is stored as a string) to `DocumentReference` at runtime:
  ```dart
  final itemRef = data['itemId'] as DocumentReference; // Fails!
  ```
- **Impact:**
  The cart screen is completely broken. It will either appear permanently empty (due to comparing String to DocumentReference) or crash immediately with a type cast exception if documents exist.
- **Solution:**
  Standardize `userId` and `itemId` to be strings across both writing and reading.

<!-- slide -->
### [Critical] Plaintext Sensitive Card Logging
- **File:** [credit_card_ui.dart](file:///c:/solcafe/lib/working%20with%20payment/credit%20card%20ui.dart#L318-L322)
- **Problem:**
  The raw card number, expiry, and CVV are printed to console logs via `print()` inside the `placingorder` method:
  ```dart
  print('Card Number: $rawCardNumber');
  print('Expiry Date: $expirydate');
  print('CVV: $cvv');
  ```
- **Impact:**
  Compromises user security and violates **PCI-DSS compliance**. These credentials can leak in production console logs, bug tracking tools, and crash reports.
- **Solution:**
  Remove the `print()` calls of sensitive card details immediately.

<!-- slide -->
### [Critical] Nested Navigation & UI Overlay
- **File:** [login.dart](file:///c:/solcafe/lib/user%20authentication/login.dart#L45-L50) & [auth_wrapper.dart](file:///c:/solcafe/lib/user%20authentication/auth%20wrapper.dart)
- **Problem:**
  On successful login, the application performs a `Navigator.pushReplacement` to `Bottomnavstylish()`. At the exact same time, `AuthWrapper` detects the auth state change and rebuilds the root view, switching it to `BottomNavHolder()`.
- **Impact:**
  This results in two duplicate trees of `Bottomnavstylish` running on top of each other. It causes double Scaffolds, duplicate page controllers, rendering anomalies, drawer errors, and broken navigation loops.
- **Solution:**
  Avoid manual routing to `Bottomnavstylish` on successful auth. Pop the auth routes or simply let `AuthWrapper` change the root view automatically.

<!-- slide -->
### [Critical] Hanged Stack on Sign Out
- **File:** [my_account.dart](file:///c:/solcafe/lib/user%20authentication/my%20account.dart#L152-L155)
- **Problem:**
  Clicking "Sign Out" triggers `signOut()` but fails to navigate the user or clean the view stack.
- **Impact:**
  The `MyAccount` screen stays at the top of the stack, but the current user is now null. The screen will crash or display null placeholder data, leaving the user with no way to return to the login interface.
- **Solution:**
  Clear the navigation stack and redirect using `pushAndRemoveUntil` when signing out:
  ```dart
  await FirebaseAuth.instance.signOut();
  Navigator.pushAndRemoveUntil(context, MaterialPageRoute(builder: (context) => const Login()), (route) => false);
  ```
```

